87327"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "CoreWeave, an AI data-center operator, delivered strong results late Tuesday. Tech stocks roared back the next morning.", "display_url": "on.wsj.com/4AvWJ0e", "end": 144, "expanded_url": "https://on.wsj.com/4AvWJ0e", "images": [{"height": 1280, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120637470131826688/pR1dPpRM?format=png&name=orig", "width": 2560}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120637470131826688/pR1dPpRM?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 121, "status": 200, "title": "Investors Run Back to AI Stocks, Less Than a Week After a Historic Selloff", "unwound_url": "https://www.wsj.com/finance/stocks/investors-run-back-to-ai-stocks-less-than-a-week-after-a-historic-selloff-854483e8?reflink=e2twmkts", "url": "https://t.co/71WE67rd6e"}]}, "id": "2120637467317387327", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5689, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Wall Street’s on-again, off-again romance with the artificial-intelligence build-out flickered back to life on Wednesday https://t.co/71WE67rd6e", "url": "https://x.com/WSJmarkets/status/2120637467317387327"}, {"author_id": "3290364847", "created_at": "2026-11-11T21:43:43.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120633596381696229"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "A study of nearly 100,000 diverse Americans identified thousands of new variants in genes that influence our responses to prescription drugs", "display_url": "trib.al/dvgqanw", "end": 164, "expanded_url": "https://trib.al/dvgqanw", "images": [{"height": 576, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120633600865456128/RjP22Af7?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1024}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120633600865456128/RjP22Af7?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 141, "status": 200, "title": "All of Us study finds thousands of new genetic variants affecting drug responses", "unwound_url": "https://www.statnews.com/2026/11/11/all-of-us-study-finds-gene-variants-drug-responses/?utm_campaign=twitter_organic&utm_source=twitter&utm_medium=social", "url": "https://t.co/RsR8MzAXBv"}]}, "id": "2120633596381696229", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 1785, "like_count": 2, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "A study of nearly 100,000 diverse Americans identified thousands of new variants in genes that influence our responses to prescription drugs https://t.co/RsR8MzAXBv", "url": "https://x.com/statnews/status/2120633596381696229"}, {"author_id": "860158302", "created_at": "2026-11-11T21:32:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120630654207475985"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "The biochemist Nick Lane thinks life first evolved in hydrothermal vents where precursors of metabolism appeared before genetic information. His ideas could lead us to think differently about aging and cancer.", "display_url": "quantamagazine.org/a-biochemists-…", "end": 137, "expanded_url": "https://www.quantamagazine.org/a-biochemists-view-of-lifes-origin-reframes-cancer-and-aging-20220808/", "start": 114, "status": 200, "title": "A Biochemist’s View of Life’s Origin Reframes Cancer and Aging | Quanta Magazine", "unwound_url": "https://www.quantamagazine.org/a-biochemists-view-of-lifes-origin-reframes-cancer-and-aging-20220808/", "url": "https://t.co/TcTaRJVN77"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/oGrGXWTBVY", "end": 161, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/QuantaMagazine/status/2120630654207475985/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120630649958621187", "start": 138, "url": "https://t.co/oGrGXWTBVY"}]}, "id": "2120630654207475985", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 16, "impression_count": 7753, "like_count": 55, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 8}, "text": "This biochemist theorizes that the essential chemistries for life may have kicked off with a very long vent sesh. https://t.co/TcTaRJVN77 https://t.co/oGrGXWTBVY", "url": "https://x.com/QuantaMagazine/status/2120630654207475985"}, {"author_id": "860158302", "created_at": "2026-11-11T21:32:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120630652324249601"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "We might have a past faint sun to owe for life’s existence. This has consequences for the possibility of life outside Earth.", "display_url": "quantamagazine.org/the-sun-was-di…", "end": 153, "expanded_url": "https://www.quantamagazine.org/the-sun-was-dimmer-when-earth-formed-how-did-life-emerge-20220127/", "start": 130, "status": 200, "title": "A Solution to the Faint-Sun Paradox Reveals a Narrow Window for Life | Quanta Magazine", "unwound_url": "https://www.quantamagazine.org/the-sun-was-dimmer-when-earth-formed-how-did-life-emerge-20220127/", "url": "https://t.co/e0P9wAMl9e"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/osPKBJsRm2", "end": 177, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/QuantaMagazine/status/2120630652324249601/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2120630650076082176", "start": 154, "url": "https://t.co/osPKBJsRm2"}]}, "id": "2120630652324249601", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 5491, "like_count": 38, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 4}, "text": "If the sun had been as powerful at Earth’s formation as it is today, our planet may have shared the dry, lifeless fate of Venus.  https://t.co/e0P9wAMl9e https://t.co/osPKBJsRm2", "url": "https://x.com/QuantaMagazine/status/2120630652324249601"}, {"author_id": "28164923", "created_at": "2026-11-11T21:27:37.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120629546026242406"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Stocks rose after CoreWeave’s earnings update quelled worries that artificial-intelligence profits would not come soon enough to cover infrastructure debt burdens.", "display_url": "on.wsj.com/4AkCS3M", "end": 82, "expanded_url": "https://on.wsj.com/4AkCS3M", "images": [{"height": 640, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2120629548261785600/LxgYzTA9?format=jpg&n